// endpoint_report_composer_entries.proto — ReportComposerEntries: the entries
// a workspace's composer holds while the person types, and the one point is
// on. FEED section.
//
// Emacs is the only sender. It reads its composer with the prompt grammar
// (tree-sitter-tldr/tldr_prompt), as the daemon reads a sent prompt, and
// reports what it reads each time it changes: the labels of every entry, in
// order, and the entry line point is on, if any. The report REPLACES the one
// before it, whole: the daemon holds the composer's entries as the last report
// stated them, never a delta.
//
// THE DAEMON ANSWERS WITH STATE, NOT IN THIS RESPONSE. From the report and
// what it already holds, it works out the response each label targets (the
// selected response bubble when one is selected, else the newest response on
// the root feed whose tree holds the label, the rule a sent prompt's entries
// are bound by), and pushes two things, each restated whenever any of their
// inputs changes (a report, the selection, a response's tree):
//   - the root feed's watch carries the node point's entry answers
//     (frontend.v1.FeedComposerEntry), which the webapp highlights;
//   - the host's watch carries the labels that target nothing
//     (agentrepl.v1.HostComposerEntries), which Emacs marks as answering
//     nothing.
//
// IDEMPOTENT: restating the entries the daemon already holds changes nothing.

